<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis IV of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 920–954</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Louis d'Outremer, Louis IV of West Francia, Louis from Overseas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis IV, called d'Outremer (&quot;from overseas&quot;), was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a> from 936 to 954. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a>, he grew up in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and was recalled to the throne with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-the-great">Hugh the Great</a>, Duke of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>. His reign was marked by struggles with Hugh and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a>, and his weak royal power foreshadowed the end of Carolingian rule in 987.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-iv-of-france.jpg" alt="Louis IV of France" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis IV (0921-0954 ; roi des Francs). Autorité émettrice de monnaie Chinon (France ; atelier monétaire). Atelier mon... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Tr%C3%A9sor_de_F%C3%A9camp,_Louis_IV_(936-954),_denier,_Chinon_-_btv1b11306996m_(transparent_version).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
